632	// synthesized clone URL (see mirrorCloneURL): if /repos ever returns the
633	// clone URL (or host) on a placement, drop it and the synthesis. It fails the
634	// whole command if unavailable rather than degrade: the clone URL is the
635	// payload of a mirror listing, and --json suppresses the stderr banner, so a
636	// degraded run would hand a script row-complete data with silently empty
637	// clone URLs and a zero exit.
